    "story_farm": {
      "type": "farm-story",
      "settings": {
        "caption": "Coffee cherries growing among the shade trees at Finca Las Nubes.",
        "image_side": "left",
        "ratio": "4 / 5",
        "eyebrow": "The farm",
        "heading": "Finca Las Nubes",
        "text": "<p>In La Dalia, Matagalpa, Finca Las Nubes covers approximately 82 hectares at elevations of 850 to 1,000 meters. The family grows Parainema, Anacafé, Catimor, and Catrenic, while introducing new varieties through ongoing planting projects.</p><p>Coffee grows under approximately 60–70% shade. The family works to preserve forested areas, trees, wildlife, and natural water sources. Traps made from recycled plastic bottles help manage pests and reduce the use of highly toxic chemicals.</p>",
        "btn_label": "",
        "btn_link": "",
        "bg": "#ffffff",
        "text_color": "#2b1208",
        "accent": "#2f5d3a",
        "btn_bg": "#3a1a0e",
        "btn_text": "#ffffff",
        "pad_top": 72,
        "pad_bottom": 72,
        "image_asset": "nicaragua-coffee-tree.jpg"
      }
